+# Dosing Modes
+
+In Trio 1.0.2, open **Settings → Dosing Mode**. This is a four-option picker, replacing the Closed Loop on/off control shown in older screenshots. Open Loop is the default. The picker requires a connected pump and an active CGM sensor session.
 
 ## What is Closed Loop?
-"Closed Loop" means Trio will use the settings and parameters you have inputted into the system to make automated insulin dosing decisions for you every 5 minutes.
 
-!!! tip
-    Trio works best as a closed loop system. If you need to test your settings, it's best to close the loop and follow the configuration [here](#want-to-stay-in-open-loop).
+**Closed Loop** allows Trio to enact its automated dosing decisions, including basal reductions, corrections and SMBs when their individual conditions and safety checks permit. A forecast is not a delivery record, and a nominal five-minute loop interval does not guarantee a dose on every cycle.
 
 ## What is Open Loop?
-"Open Loop" means Trio cannot make any adjustments automatically. In open loop, the system relies solely on you to make any adjustments.  
 
-You can control your pump and bolus with the Trio app, but nothing can be done without your approval. This is often referred to as running in open loop. You will get no Trio-initiated protection from lows or highs while in open loop. Trio essentially becomes a fancy non-AID PDM with a bolus calculator.
+**Open Loop** displays forecasts and recommendations without enacting automated dosing. Your pump continues its scheduled basal delivery. Manual bolus commands are separate user actions. Open Loop does not provide Trio-initiated low-glucose suspension or automatic correction of highs.
+
+## Low Glucose Suspend
+
+**Low Glucose Suspend (LGS)** permits predictive basal reductions while treating effective Max IOB as 0. Your saved Max IOB preference is preserved. It is not a fixed glucose-trigger switch. If reduced basal has produced negative IOB, insulin may be replenished until IOB reaches zero; therefore this mode should not be described as forbidding every amount above the scheduled basal rate.
+
+## Basal Testing
+
+**Basal Testing** permits low-glucose suspension rather than normal algorithm adjustments. It derives effective Max IOB 0, Autosens Min/Max 100%, Dynamic ISF off, and sigmoid off. Its threshold preference is at least 72 mg/dL: `max(saved threshold, 72)`. Profile generation also enables the suspend-only behavior. Entering this mode attempts to cancel an existing automatic temporary basal, subject to pump and delivery-state checks.
+
+These are temporary, derived mode constraints. They do not overwrite the saved preferences. Returning to another mode can restore the influence of those saved settings.
 
 ## Want to stay in Open Loop?
-Many users feel the need to stay in open loop initially for a variety of reasons, such as testing settings or weariness about a new algorithm. It is not advised to keep the loop open with Trio due to the significant loss in functionality. Rather, configure the following settings as such:
 
-<div class="grid cards" markdown>
-    
--   - Set [Max IOB](therapy/units-limits.md#max-iob) to **0**
-    - Set [Autosens Max](algorithm/autosens.md#autosens-max) to **100%**
-    - Set [Autosens Min](algorithm/autosens.md#autosens-min) to **100%**
-    - All other [Algorithm Settings](algorithm/index.md) should remain at their defaults if you are a new user
+Choose a mode by its actual automation behavior. Use the descriptions above to distinguish no automated enactment, predictive reductions, low-only suspension and full automation. The earlier recipe that changed saved Max IOB and Autosens values is not the dedicated Basal Testing mode. It should not be presented as equivalent to that mode.
 
--   !!! tip "Existing Users"
-    If you are an existing user making these adjustments for testing your settings, Algorithm Settings can remain as you had them previously configured. Keep in mind: you may need to adjust them after your settings test is completed if there are significant changes made to your Core Trio Settings (basal, ISF, CR).
-
-</div>
-
-This will allow Trio to continue communications with your pump and CGM uninterrupted. Setting Max IOB this way will allow Trio to prevent lows by reducing basal, but will not allow Trio to treat highs automatically. Setting Autosens Max and Min this way will stop all algorithm sensitivity adjustments, and Trio will only utilize your profile settings as you entered them. This will significantly hinder the algorithm, turning it into a non-dynamic system with only low-prevention. This is much safer than attempting to run in open loop.
-
-!!! caution "Former Loop Users"
-    Loop and Trio function differently in open loop due to the differences in the underlying algorithms. It is rarely advised to stay in open loop with Trio, as most of the functionality of the algorithm depends on a closed loop system.
+The mode applies to automated enactment; it is not a blanket block on every manually requested or remotely requested bolus. Those paths have their own controls and validation.
 
 
